WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.531
When I woke up the next morning, I could hear Mom in the kitchen.

2
00:00:18.532 --> 00:00:22.863
I sniffed the air. Mmm . . .

3
00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:27.720
Pancakes! Tate was already at the table, eating breakfast.

4
00:00:27.721 --> 00:00:32.229
"Hey," I said. "Save some pancakes for me!"

5
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.790
Tate made a face at me.

6
00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:37.524
"Iggy," said Mom with a frown.

7
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:40.540
"Please say good morning to your brother."

8
00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:46.006
"But Mom," I started to argue. "He made a face–"

9
00:00:46.007 --> 00:00:49.937
Before I could finish telling her, the telephone rang.

10
00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:52.533
Then the doorbell rang.

11
00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.064
My mom answered the telephone.

12
00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:58.504
"What?" she said, sounding surprised.

13
00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:01.196
"Really? How wonderful!"

14
00:01:01.197 --> 00:01:02.865
I answered the door.

15
00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:05.202
It was Josh and Jenny.

16
00:01:05.203 --> 00:01:09.806
"You'll never guess what happened!" Jenny cried.

17
00:01:09.807 --> 00:01:12.496
I could hear Mom in the kitchen.

18
00:01:12.497 --> 00:01:15.621
"Wait until I tell Iggy!" she said.

19
00:01:15.622 --> 00:01:18.071
"He'll be so excited!"

20
00:01:18.072 --> 00:01:20.880
So much was happening at once.

21
00:01:20.881 --> 00:01:25.301
"Bunch's ticket won the raffle!" said Josh.

22
00:01:25.302 --> 00:01:32.171
"We got a telephone call this morning from a hotel—the Shadow Lake Lodge," added Jenny.

23
00:01:32.172 --> 00:01:35.540
"We're all going to the mountain getaway!"

24
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:39.179
I was so surprised, my mouth fell open.

25
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.221
"Oh boy!" I whooped.

26
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:46.157
"Molly and Caswell can come too," said Josh.

27
00:01:46.158 --> 00:01:47.405
"That makes six.

28
00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:50.092
Plus Bunch because he's the winner!"

29
00:01:50.093 --> 00:01:55.977
"The Lodge said we have to keep him in a dog cage in our room," said Jenny.

30
00:01:55.978 --> 00:01:59.492
Josh, Jenny, and I ran into the kitchen.

31
00:01:59.493 --> 00:02:02.711
"Thank you for calling," my mom was saying.

32
00:02:02.712 --> 00:02:05.452
"The kids will be so excited."

33
00:02:05.453 --> 00:02:07.731
She hung up the telephone.

34
00:02:07.732 --> 00:02:13.209
"That was Mr. Chen," she said. "You're all going–"

35
00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.558
"To the mountain getaway!"

36
00:02:15.559 --> 00:02:18.900
Josh, Jenny, and I cried at the same time.

37
00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:22.948
"Yes," said Mom, laughing.

38
00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:27.365
"Bunch's raffle ticket was chosen, so he's the winner!"

39
00:02:27.366 --> 00:02:31.279
"Which means we're the winners!" I said.

40
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.899
"My dad says we can go next weekend," said Jenny.

41
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.103
At that moment the wheels in my head started to turn.

42
00:02:40.104 --> 00:02:43.557
I needed an idea for a new invention.

43
00:02:43.558 --> 00:02:48.759
I wanted it to be a special invention for our mountain getaway.

44
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.626
"Mom, Iggy's getting weird again," said Tate.

45
00:02:52.627 --> 00:02:55.553
"He's got that look on his face."

46
00:02:55.554 --> 00:02:58.367
"What look?" asked Josh.

47
00:02:58.368 --> 00:03:03.367
"The look that means he's about to make a huge mess," said Tate.

48
00:03:03.368 --> 00:03:10.287
Mom laughed. "Iggy's probably thinking up a new invention."

49
00:03:10.288 --> 00:03:15.366
"Which means he's about to make a mess, just like I said!" said Tate.

50
00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:18.497
He grinned and punched me in the arm.

51
00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:21.253
I punched him back playfully.

52
00:03:21.254 --> 00:03:24.893
"Tate really isn't such a bad brother," I thought.

53
00:03:24.894 --> 00:03:29.475
Maybe we wouldn't fight as much now that we didn't share a room anymore.

54
00:03:29.476 --> 00:03:33.970
Josh, Jenny, and I ran over to Molly and Caswell's apartment.

55
00:03:33.971 --> 00:03:37.070
We wanted to tell them the big news.

56
00:03:37.071 --> 00:03:39.398
"Wow!" said Molly.

57
00:03:39.399 --> 00:03:42.912
"I'm going to bring my new sleeping bag!"

58
00:03:42.913 --> 00:03:46.527
"I'm going to bring my backpack," said Caswell.

59
00:03:46.528 --> 00:03:47.862
"And my flashlight.

60
00:03:47.863 --> 00:03:52.422
We might get lost in the woods in the middle of the night."

61
00:03:52.423 --> 00:03:54.449
We all laughed.

62
00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:58.542
"I don't think we're going to get lost in the woods," said Josh.

63
00:03:58.543 --> 00:04:01.156
"Especially in the middle of the night."

64
00:04:01.157 --> 00:04:04.608
Suddenly the wheels in my head started spinning again.

65
00:04:04.609 --> 00:04:08.954
But this time my mind went click!

66
00:04:08.955 --> 00:04:13.041
Now I had an idea for my new invention!

67
00:04:13.042 --> 00:04:16.468
I didn't tell anyone about it—not yet.

68
00:04:16.469 --> 00:04:19.697
First I had to see how it was going to work.

69
00:04:19.698 --> 00:04:23.723
I started by borrowing hamster pellets from Josh.

70
00:04:23.724 --> 00:04:27.102
Next I asked Mom for some food coloring.

71
00:04:27.103 --> 00:04:31.858
She gave me red, green, blue, and yellow.

72
00:04:31.859 --> 00:04:35.814
Then I went into my room and closed the door.

73
00:04:35.815 --> 00:04:41.168
I, Iggy, was about to invent something that would amaze the world.

74
00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:48.241
And it would keep people from getting stranded in the mountains!
